  ('cf76d96b-75b7-5609-b71a-1192bfdcd318', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Okada motorcycle taxis took their name from which defunct airline?', '["Bellview Airlines","Okada Air","Nigeria Airways","Kabo Air"]'::jsonb, 1, 4, 'Okada Air was based in Benin City.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okada_Air', 'live'),
  ('745048ab-0580-5172-80e4-71b160c2971c', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Covenant University, linked to Winners Chapel, is in which state?', '["Kwara","Oyo","Lagos","Ogun"]'::jsonb, 3, 4, 'It sits inside Canaanland in Ota.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Covenant_University', 'live'),
  ('69d7f27e-b6ab-5936-ba90-7bf1bfb56023', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'The Yoruba engagement ceremony is called?', '["Igba nkwu","Ofala","Kamu","Idana"]'::jsonb, 3, 4, 'Families exchange gifts and the bride price.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoruba_people', 'in_review'),
  ('cd6e5a78-5c1a-5805-8071-bd8faf7b5df9', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Abuja''s registered taxis are traditionally painted which colours?', '["Red and white","Green and white","Yellow and black","Blue and white"]'::jsonb, 1, 4, 'The colours echo the national flag.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Abuja', 'in_review'),
  ('13c2be7f-1032-591c-9f01-b59166bbfb66', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'In northern Nigeria, motorcycle taxis are commonly called?', '["Molue","Danfo","Achaba","Kabu kabu"]'::jsonb, 2, 4, 'Several northern states have restricted them.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Okada_(motorcycle_taxi)', 'in_review'),
  ('e918aa2b-36df-52e8-9f33-24ea9f1060cb', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'What is Nigeria''s national emergency phone number?', '["199","112","911","999"]'::jsonb, 1, 4, 'Some states also run their own lines, like Lagos''s 767.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emergency_telephone_number', 'in_review'),
  ('c6067e89-9056-59a0-8dce-85ccffbb1827', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', '''Babban riga'' is a flowing robe worn by men of which people?', '["Hausa and Fulani","Igbo","Ijaw","Tiv"]'::jsonb, 0, 4, 'Its name means ''big gown'' in Hausa.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boubou_(clothing)', 'in_review'),
  ('35f75f18-c998-5204-9fab-df293e577f10', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which Lagos military administrator introduced the ''Keke'' tricycles?', '["Raji Rasaki","Buba Marwa","Olagunsoye Oyinlola","Ahmed Mohammed"]'::jsonb, 1, 5, 'He governed Lagos from 1996 to 1999.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohammed_Buba_Marwa', 'live'),
  ('847d7361-eae7-5e77-b08b-1eab42306ccc', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'The 1983 order expelling West African migrants, which gave the ''Ghana Must Go'' bag its name, was issued under which president?', '["Olusegun Obasanjo","Muhammadu Buhari","Shehu Shagari","Ibrahim Babangida"]'::jsonb, 2, 5, 'Over a million people, many of them Ghanaian, had to leave.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ghana_Must_Go', 'live'),
  ('5a17ac09-b07e-5f70-94d4-328de1f9201b', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which Lagos expressway hosts the Redemption Camp and the Mountain of Fire prayer city?', '["Lagos–Ibadan Expressway","Ikorodu Road","Badagry Expressway","Third Mainland Bridge"]'::jsonb, 0, 5, 'The stretch is often called the world''s busiest ''church road''.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagos%E2%80%93Ibadan_Expressway', 'live'),
  ('56121254-4691-53c9-8e5c-da4ac4c3cc6d', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which Lagos BRT corridor was the first, opened in 2008?', '["Lekki to Ajah","Oshodi to Abule Egba","Ikorodu to TBS","Mile 12 to CMS"]'::jsonb, 3, 5, 'It was the first BRT system in sub-Saharan Africa.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagos_Bus_Rapid_Transit_System', 'live'),
  ('b5e21539-e367-51b9-a0b9-951ef3b50a44', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which Lagos emergency number did the state set up for its own emergencies?', '["199","911","112","767"]'::jsonb, 3, 5, 'Lagos also runs 112 alongside it.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagos_State', 'in_review'),
  ('31e7a78d-e047-5ae0-a97a-fcbc73dcbc25', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'What does FRSC stand for?', '["Federal Rail Service Company","Federal Roads and Streets Commission","Free Road Speed Control","Federal Road Safety Corps"]'::jsonb, 3, 1, 'FRSC officials patrol highways and issue driver''s licences.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Road_Safety_Corps', 'live'),
  ('340c3611-8fba-585e-bb8b-2609d254af87', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which messaging app do most Nigerians use daily?', '["WeChat","Telegram","Signal","WhatsApp"]'::jsonb, 3, 1, 'Family WhatsApp groups are a Nigerian institution.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_Nigeria', 'live'),
  ('dacdf9d6-96ec-50a5-95f7-cfc8db280df3', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Linda Ikeji is best known as a…', '["Footballer","Governor","Blogger","Singer"]'::jsonb, 2, 1, 'Her celebrity news blog made her one of Nigeria''s richest bloggers.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linda_Ikeji', 'live'),
  ('c5158cfd-69f2-568d-abe2-f14232eeb82b', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which basic phone feature earned some handsets the nickname ''torchlight phones''?', '["A radio","A built-in flashlight","A camera","A solar panel"]'::jsonb, 1, 1, 'They are loved for their long-lasting batteries.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_Nigeria', 'live'),
  ('b9f867b3-4626-5a53-b59b-11466301e194', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'MTN''s long-running slogan is?', '["The smartphone network","Life is better","Everywhere you go","Rule your world"]'::jsonb, 2, 1, 'MTN''s yellow is one of Nigeria''s best-known brand colours.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MTN_Nigeria', 'live'),
  ('b3793be7-7fac-5a1f-a35f-dd132f301a92', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'What does LASTMA stand for?', '["Lagos State Transport and Motor Agency","Lagos State Taxi Management Association","Lagos Area Street Traffic Marshals","Lagos State Traffic Management Authority"]'::jsonb, 3, 2, 'LASTMA officials direct traffic across Lagos.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lagos_State_Traffic_Management_Authority', 'live'),
  ('ea7f388f-1657-5960-942a-40a5df8e4de5', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Federal Government Colleges are popularly called?', '["Federal Academies","Model Schools","Grammar Schools","Unity Schools"]'::jsonb, 3, 2, 'They bring together students from every state.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Government_College', 'live'),
  ('39a41136-bb2a-581d-a505-3ad099d4b98a', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'In Nigerian universities, a ''2:1'' is…', '["First Class","Third Class","Second Class Lower","Second Class Upper"]'::jsonb, 3, 2, 'A ''2:2'' is Second Class Lower.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/British_undergraduate_degree_classification', 'live'),
  ('45ae1396-960a-5f56-9662-41effb7f73fe', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'What does HND stand for?', '["Higher Nigerian Degree","Higher National Diploma","Higher National Doctorate","Honours National Diploma"]'::jsonb, 1, 2, 'HNDs are awarded by polytechnics.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Higher_National_Diploma', 'live'),
  ('861b672f-0180-5436-8ebd-5868c9c56e28', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'In Yoruba culture, men traditionally greet elders by doing what?', '["Kneeling","Prostrating (dọ̀bálẹ̀)","Bowing slightly","Hugging"]'::jsonb, 1, 2, 'Women traditionally kneel (kúnlẹ̀).', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoruba_people', 'live'),
  ('99d5edf9-3d6f-599a-a6be-2e884dbc8533', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'An Egungun is a Yoruba…', '["Talking drum","Wedding dress","Ancestral masquerade","Market day"]'::jsonb, 2, 2, 'Egungun festivals honour the dead.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Egungun', 'live'),
  ('99e39345-8fb1-51f2-a40e-f1eb41f50318', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Lagos''s Eyo masquerades are famous for wearing which colour?', '["Black","Red","White","Green"]'::jsonb, 2, 2, 'They wear white robes and wide-brimmed hats.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eyo_festival', 'live'),
  ('8878cff2-54f3-5638-a172-dc4f85b3c150', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', '''Okrika'' clothes are…', '["School uniforms","Second-hand clothes","Wedding gowns","Brand-new designer wear"]'::jsonb, 1, 2, 'They are also called ''bend-down select''.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_Nigeria', 'live'),
  ('b3265eb9-f7f6-59bc-afd9-1e22a5d92d4c', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'A ''kabu kabu'' is…', '["An unlicensed taxi","A night market","A type of drum","A fast boat"]'::jsonb, 0, 2, 'Kabu kabu drivers often use private cars.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Culture_of_Nigeria', 'live'),
  ('bf6161a3-ebd5-5a61-8331-76f60453f605', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Street currency changers in Nigeria are often popularly called?', '["Aboki (or mallam) FX","Danfo traders","Agberos","Corpers"]'::jsonb, 0, 2, 'Many operate near hotels and airports.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bureau_de_change', 'live'),
  ('fdca71f2-3da4-5706-b939-e0c0a32cf157', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Which Chinese company makes the Tecno and Itel phones popular in Nigeria?', '["Lenovo","Xiaomi","Transsion","Huawei"]'::jsonb, 2, 2, 'Transsion is one of Africa''s biggest phone sellers.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transsion', 'live'),
  ('a6a2918c-a9c7-5f2e-a6ca-0ed69f301548', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'What type of electrical plug is most common in Nigeria?', '["Type G (three square pins)","Type C (two round pins)","Type I (angled pins)","Type A (two flat pins)"]'::jsonb, 0, 3, 'It is the same plug used in the UK.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AC_power_plugs_and_sockets', 'live'),
  ('54ca6732-949f-52d6-8e07-3080c52fa366', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'The ''Oga at the top'' meme came from a 2013 TV interview with an official of which agency?', '["Immigration","Civil Defence (NSCDC)","Police","Customs"]'::jsonb, 1, 3, 'He could not name his agency''s website.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nigeria_Security_and_Civil_Defence_Corps', 'live'),
  ('7d8c83b0-a702-511d-91f6-8ec5b7cdd50c', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'In Igbo families, the first son is called?', '["Obi","Nwanne","Okpara","Ada"]'::jsonb, 2, 3, 'The first daughter is called Ada.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igbo_people', 'live'),
  ('0a7833f2-f3c6-57d4-95bd-2cd1ec7bc68e', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'The Fulani ''Sharo'' festival tests young men''s…', '["Wrestling","Bravery, through flogging","Horse riding","Singing"]'::jsonb, 1, 3, 'Young men endure lashes without flinching to prove manhood.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sharo_(Fulani_tradition)', 'live'),
  ('4df8b060-71b0-5933-b2d5-a9acc359a995', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', '''Mmanwu'' is the Igbo word for?', '["Market","Elder","Masquerade","Palm wine"]'::jsonb, 2, 3, 'Mmanwu festivals feature colourful masked spirits.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igbo_people', 'live'),
  ('49079c20-1ba5-51ce-9df9-0dd4d5417cb8', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Lagos''s CMS bus stop is named after which organisation?', '["Central Market Society","City Motor Service","Church Missionary Society","Commercial Marine Station"]'::jsonb, 2, 3, 'The CMS founded Nigeria''s oldest secondary school.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Church_Mission_Society', 'live'),
  ('ccbee581-4815-5d76-85af-67ee81f7a2d6', '3aa4c1e6-7ac4-5d8c-8926-6e09ec7be605', 'Nairaland, a huge Nigerian online forum, was founded by?', '["Sim Shagaya","Jason Njoku","Linda Ikeji","Seun Osewa"]'::jsonb, 3, 3, 'It launched in 2005.', 'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nairaland', 'live')
